    "result_text": "The full suite consists of the single `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes `POST /api/owners` (and any Owner response) return a `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo small, well-placed edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field. It lives on `Owner`, not `OwnerFields`, keeping it a response-only derived value (not an editable input).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`. Formatting is derived at the DTO boundary where the mapper already owns entity\u2192DTO translation, so no entity, function step, or persistence logic had to change.\n\nThe test creates an owner and reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, expecting `$.displayName == \"LastName, John\"` \u2014 green.",
